  "source": {
    "id": "jlr-scanner-kline-route-hypotheses",
    "title": "Hypothesis: the K-line buses of the L322 and the L316 are reached through the adapter's routes k-line-7 and k-line-8",
    "source_type": "unverified_research",
    "origin": "JLR Scanner reasoning over the SDD platform documents' <iso> buses, the MongoosePro JLR user guide's pinout and the firmware's own status texts (ADR-0029)",
    "source_locator": "repository:docs/adr/ADR-0029-k-line-ds2-and-kwp2000-for-the-legacy-buses.md",
    "content_fingerprint": null,
    "acquired_on": "2026-09-12",
    "declared_vehicle_programs": [],
    "provenance": "Not a documented fact. The platform documents state, for four of the six K-line buses, the J1962 pin the bus is on: DS2_PIN7 and KW2000 on pin 7, KW2000STAR_PIN8 and ROSCO on pin 8. The adapter's firmware opens resources 3 and 4 and answers a wrong pin pair with 'supports ISO9141 K line on pin 3, 7 or 8'; its user guide gives the JLR variant K-Line on pin 7 and ROSCO on pin 8. Hence the hypothesis that a bus on pin 7 is carried by route k-line-7 and a bus on pin 8 by route k-line-8 — the pin is the document's, the route is the hypothesis, because this adapter has never opened a K-line with a pin selected. Two buses, DS2 and KW2000STAR, state no pin at all: they are hypothesised on pin 7 through k-line-7 on a weaker footing — the same documents name DS2_PIN7 for the one module they had to place explicitly, and the user guide gives K-Line on pin 7 — and are refuted the day a module on one of them answers on pin 8. Confirmed by the first read-only answer from a module on the bus; refuted by its absence.",
    "redistribution_status": "permitted",
    "notes": "Records here resolve as Unverified and the survey shows them as a hypothesis, never as a reachable route. Until the second slice of ADR-0029 opens a K-line on the adapter, no request travels on these routes at all."
  },
